{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01474",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 2.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "good afternoon, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.76,
      "end_seconds": 12.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.76,
      "end_seconds": 22.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Mainly a dry cough in the evenings. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.74,
      "end_seconds": 25.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.31,
      "end_seconds": 28.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Probably about a month. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.34,
      "end_seconds": 37.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.94,
      "end_seconds": 46.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "it's a few times a day. A six out of ten, I suppose. Pollen season definitely sets it off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.82,
      "end_seconds": 50.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.78,
      "end_seconds": 58.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "It usually comes with itchy eyes. The itchy eyes? That's been for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.48,
      "end_seconds": 67.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.37,
      "end_seconds": 70.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Loratadine, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.76,
      "end_seconds": 73.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.78,
      "end_seconds": 79.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "10 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.89,
      "end_seconds": 83.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.9,
      "end_seconds": 89.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "um, no, I've never been operated on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.78,
      "end_seconds": 94.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.42,
      "end_seconds": 100.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.75,
      "end_seconds": 106.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.14,
      "end_seconds": 120.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago. I only drink at family occasions. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.84,
      "end_seconds": 135.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.7,
      "end_seconds": 139.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.46,
      "end_seconds": 142.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Have you had any wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.9,
      "end_seconds": 149.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Not at all, no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.72,
      "end_seconds": 154.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Right, and what about fever or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.46,
      "end_seconds": 159.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "no, none that I've noticed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.04,
      "end_seconds": 165.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.1,
      "end_seconds": 170.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.63,
      "end_seconds": 175.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.07,
      "end_seconds": 186.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.52,
      "end_seconds": 210.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "okay: respiratory rate 18, pressure 125 over 74, SpO2 99 percent on room air. And temp 36.4 degrees, heart rate 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.66,
      "end_seconds": 216.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.32,
      "end_seconds": 218.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.25,
      "end_seconds": 237.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your nose looks a little swollen inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.4,
      "end_seconds": 245.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.81,
      "end_seconds": 271.03,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it's hard to say. Seasonal hay fever causing the cough is one possibility and early asthma another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.81,
      "end_seconds": 291.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "I'm going to to put you on fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That's for hay fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.8,
      "end_seconds": 295.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.4,
      "end_seconds": 316.11,
      "duration_seconds": 18.71,
      "text": "Keep windows closed on high-pollen days and wash your hair at night. Please don't wait if you start wheezing. That's when to be seen urgently. Come back in a month. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.68,
      "end_seconds": 328.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.29,
      "text": "So, I take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.78,
      "end_seconds": 336.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.68,
      "end_seconds": 340.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    }
  ]
}